{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405202-how-are-souls-created-how-do-reincarnated-hun-souls-get-new-po-souls","id":1405202,"title":"How are souls created? How do reincarnated Hun souls get new Po souls?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-29T14:34:41-07:00","id":1405202,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How are souls created? How do reincarnated Hun souls get new Po souls?","content":"<i>Science</i> of the SOUL!<br /> <br /> Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> I love how human souls work in Creation, but a lot of what I thought I know is speculation.<br /> <br /> Has this ever been covered in any Edition?<br /> <br /> How are souls born in Creation?<br /> <br /> Are souls born as a mechanical part of the Loom of Fate?<br /> <br /> How do reincarnated Hun souls get new Po souls?<br /> <br /> Hun souls can easily &amp; permanently lose their Po souls when they reincarnate, leaving a Po soul in the Underworld. They have a new Po when they reincarnate. I always assumed they grow a new one, but I'm not sure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T14:58:20-07:00","id":1405204,"title":"","content":"Souls (of both kinds, I assume) come from the Well of Souls, which is... somewhere. Possibly literally in the peak of Mount Meru. I believe that was where the First Edition Autochthonians book described the eight champions acquiring the ones to fill the Ewer, but even apart from that being in a prior Edition I'd say it depends on how literally you take it.<br /> <br /> It's my understanding that the natural state of Po souls is to remain behind with the body as a kind of quiescent and satisfied equivalent to the hungry ghost but which still might be provoked, and ultimately just fades away as the body decays. Residence in the Underworld is reserved for those that became hungry ghosts and then managed to find their way in through a shadowland.<br /> <br /> Hun souls gathered by Heaven pass through Lethe on their way to a new destination, and it's my understanding that even to the gods this is largely a black box of a process; they don't really understand how it works nor can fully tangibly identify mechanisms involved in it. It's connected enough to the Celestial Bureaucracy that there's some level of process by which the destination of a particular soul can be influenced (this can be found in things like one of the Sidereal Resplendencies or the whole idea in Lands of Creation that the Solar Deliberative legislated for favourable reincarnation to be granted to those whose lives were lost in their service or to their indulgences), but I get the impression that is also something where they don't quite get where those instructions are going or how they're being processed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T15:14:42-07:00","id":1405205,"title":"","content":"In one 1E adeventure, when Autochthon reawakens he consumes a massive number of souls to restore his energy reserves. This causes something like half the stars in the sky to go out because the firmament was the Well of Souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T03:29:56-07:00","id":1405291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405202-how-are-souls-created-how-do-reincarnated-hun-souls-get-new-po-souls?p=1405205#post1405205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one 1E adeventure, when Autochthon reawakens he consumes a massive number of souls to restore his energy reserves. This causes something like half the stars in the sky to go out because the firmament was the Well of Souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that was the revelation in one of the scenarios. I imagine it had a tighter connection to Lethe before the Great War, and the Stars are also a reflection of the Loom of Fate and the Life of Gods.<br /> <br /> <br /> Later there is talk that Souls were woven from the Wyld by the Well, but after they have enough souls they just recycle Hun souls so each soul has a legacy of past lives and rarely are new souls made.<br /> <br /> Outside of Autochthonia Po souls are new for each life. Po souls might not even come from the Well of Souls, they might be more directly created from the Wyld. We don't have much of an explanation of whether the Well of Souls covers all types of souls or mostly just human hun souls. In Autobot they recycle and reuse so they keep the Hun and Po together if they can via soul gems and releasing them into the Gears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T08:16:58-07:00","id":1405340,"title":"","content":"My usual take is that Po' souls, that being a more basal/animalistic kind of soul and, as portrayed by hungry ghosts and their strong connection to their corpses, are a product of the body per se and part of the arcane/biological processes that make it up for both animals and sapient beings. It's the Hun/higher soul, a key element of what composes the mind/identity/intelect of a sapient being, where things get tricky with reincarnation/recycling and all those funny spiritual processes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-30-2020, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T02:13:58-07:00","id":1406238,"title":"","content":"The following is 150% headcanon based on partial understanding of written sources. Treat it as such, but FWIW it's how I run souls.<br /> <br /> Lethe is the name given to the proper functioning of the reincarnation of human souls. People are born with an upper (Hun) and lower (Po) soul. The Hun soul is deposited out of Lethe when the person is born, the Po soul is created and gifted to the child by their parents - it is also the Essential mechanism by which supernatural lineage (ie God bloods) is passed to the next generation without a specific &quot;genetic&quot; biological alternative.<br /> <br /> When someone dies the lower soul vanishes into the earth if properly buried (else becoming a hungry ghost) and the upper soul enters Lethe and is reborn. Those who evade Lethe either by choice or chance are flung into the Underworld and become ghosts. Lethe isn't tangible like other realms of existence. Not even Exalts can &quot;go there&quot;; though some Exalts retain memories of past lives, and ghosts are an aberration from 'something', so it must exist. But is it a place like the river Styx, a process like reincarnation, a person/personification like the Grim Reaper guiding souls? Nobody knows, not even the mightiest Gods or Exalted. <br /> <br /> I have two main theories on Lethe, which I refer to as:<br /> <b>1) Bucket of Marbles - </b>Each Hun soul is unique and permanent. When someone is born, Fate reaches into the bucket and pulls out a marble (soul) at random and it becomes a living person. When they die, the marble goes back in the bucket, to eventually be reincarnated in a new person. It's always the same soul, so you are the next link in a chain stretching back to infinity.<br /> <br /> <b>2) Bucket of Water - </b>Each time a human is born a spoonful of water (soul) is taken out of the bucket. When the person dies the spoonful of water goes back. Unlike the above, you will never be able to get that exact same spoonful back from the bucket, you may get part of it, a few drops, but never the whole thing. So reincarnation here is in the form of a collective human consciousness which develops with each generation, but no specific individual who existed will ever be reborn whole. Instead anyone or everyone may share part of their soul; this is where the idea of soulmates comes from.<br /> <br /> I prefer the latter, with Marbles applying to beings with perfect reincarnation like Dragon Kings. The exception to Bucket of Water being some sort of working which freezes your spoonful of water into a perpetual ice cube so you alone reincarnate perfectly like Misho in Keychain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T07:14:56-07:00","id":1406268,"title":"","content":"It's implied that the underworld existed even before the deaths of the neverborn in 3e, so it might be that ghosts were always a natural transition period for souls to some extent, except that with the underworld cut off from creation entirely the process of shedding worldly attachments may have been much quicker.<br /> <br /> The Water vs marbles analogy is interesting, because the way alchemicals work implies marbles, but there's the whole soul gem business going on which can easily be pointed at as a &quot;working&quot; that alters autocthonian souls this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T14:47:23-07:00","id":1406332,"title":"","content":"I had a headcanon for how new human souls are created (not for the storing of thosevalready in circulation) if anyone wants me to dig it out of the headcanon thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}